Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.00,Header,,0,0,0,,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.78,0:00:05.70,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,450,4580,4900)\pos(653.755,324.455)}Episode 61
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.78,0:00:05.70,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,450,4580,4900)\pos(653.755,524.455)}Cáo Pī Usurps the Hàn
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.20,0:00:20.32,Thinking,,0,0,0,,After King Cao Cao of Wei died, \NHua Xin and other officials
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.32,0:00:27.66,Thinking,,0,0,0,,made Cao Pi the new King of Wei,\N Chancellor, and Governor of Ji Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.90,0:00:31.94,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,500,1700,2020)\pos(342,514)}Cáo Pī\NStyled: Zǐhuán
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.94,0:00:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.49,0:00:38.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, please! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.56,0:00:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.22,0:00:46.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The Marquis of Yanling has come with \Na hundred thousand troops for the funeral!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.63,0:00:56.14,Default,,0,0,0,,My yellow-bearded little brother \Nhas always been fierce by nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.72,0:00:59.15,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He is a military prodigy \Nand now comes with an army.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.15,0:01:01.52,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He must want to fight me for the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.84,0:01:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What can be done about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.72,0:01:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.99,0:01:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I request to see the Marquis of Yanling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.92,0:01:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,If he is admonished with\N righteous words, he will submit.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.50,0:01:20.30,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1380,1980)\pos(979.2,465.6)}Jiǎ Kuí\NStyled: Liángdào
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.56,0:01:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, this crisis cannot be averted by anyone but Minister Jia.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.83,0:01:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, please go immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.37,0:01:32.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, please rest assured.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.52,0:01:45.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I, Jia Kui, welcome the Marquis of Yanling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.59,0:01:49.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is the late King's jade seal?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.38,0:01:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,A home has an eldest son; \Na state has an heir.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.19,0:01:56.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The late King's jade seal is not for you to inquire about.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.58,0:01:56.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1420,1980)\pos(950.4,464)}Cáo Zhāng\NStyled: Zǐwén
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.84,0:02:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Enter the city!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.12,0:02:09.31,Default,,0,0,0,,-Welcome, Your Highness!\N-Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.21,0:02:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you come for the funeral or do you come for the throne?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.96,0:02:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,For the funeral! I have no other intentions!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.23,0:02:20.43,Default,,0,0,0,,If you have no other intentions, why enter the city with troops?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.43,0:02:21.10,Default,,0,0,0,,That...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.73,0:02:34.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Stand down!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.30,0:02:42.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.31,0:02:51.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Greetings, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.85,0:02:55.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Little Brother, please get up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.96,0:02:59.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.08,0:03:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Little Brother, how are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.36,0:03:04.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.00,0:03:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.33,0:03:08.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.24,0:03:14.67,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Using a ploy, Cao Pi seized the army of Cao Zhang, Marquis of Yanling,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.67,0:03:17.52,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and ordered him to return to Yanling to defend himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.58,0:03:21.40,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Cao Zhi, the Marquis of Linzi, did not go to the funeral.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.40,0:03:25.44,Thinking,,0,0,0,,This infuriated Cao Pi, who sent an envoy to condemn him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.39,0:03:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Come, drink!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.33,0:03:32.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Lordship!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.11,0:03:34.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The envoy of the King of Wei is here!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.56,0:03:39.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Drink!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.86,0:03:41.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Come! Drink!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.67,0:03:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Lordship, the King of Wei...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.37,0:03:53.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I was born in a troubled world and grew up in the army.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.30,0:03:56.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,6180,6540)\pos(308.8,484.8)}Cáo Zhí\NStyled: Zǐjiàn
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.84,0:04:11.20,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Excerpt from {\i1}White Horse{\i0} (白馬篇), a historical poem by Cao Zhi.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.84,0:04:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}"Given he has the body to the blade.\NFor nary a time does he cleave to life."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.10,0:04:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Pay no heed does he for his family\Nlesser still does he to children or wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.21,0:04:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}\NFor he is in the annals of the bold; \NFor no selfish whims can him sway or hold
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.93,0:04:39.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}His life he gives to relieve the nation;\Nand look on death akin a journey home.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.84,0:04:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.19,0:05:02.89,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}\NFor he is in the annals of the bold; \NFor no selfish whims can him sway or hold
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.89,0:05:19.65,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}His life he gives to relieve the nation;\Nand look on death akin a journey home.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.59,0:05:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Lordship!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.33,0:05:41.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The King of Wei is admonishing you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.67,0:05:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,After your father's death, why did you not go to his funeral?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.42,0:05:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,The late King intended to pass the throne to my master,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.34,0:05:51.42,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1700,2060)\pos(316.8,486.4)}Dīng Yí\NStyled: Zhènglǐ
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.81,0:05:54.48,Default,,0,0,0,,but was hindered by slandering officials!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.48,0:05:58.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Admonishing kin just after the passing of the late King...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.97,0:06:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is the reason in that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.63,0:06:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,My master is gifted beyond measure. \NHe should have the throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.91,0:06:07.27,Default,,0,0,0,,and yet he does not.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.27,0:06:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,You courtiers are blind to true talent!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.88,0:06:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You... you... you!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.15,0:06:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Men!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.42,0:06:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.37,0:06:17.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Beat him out of the house!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.05,0:06:23.14,Default,,0,0,0,,How reckless!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.38,0:06:27.03,Default,,0,0,0,,How was I beaten?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.03,0:06:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,He was beating you, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.40,0:06:32.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Tiger Lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.78,0:06:33.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.94,0:06:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Lead three thousand Tiger Guards to Linzi!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.09,0:06:38.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Capture the Marquis and his lot!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.06,0:06:38.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.38,0:06:45.06,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1300,1660)\pos(966.4,467.2)}Xú Zhǔ\NStyled: Zhòngkāng
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.88,0:06:44.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Detain them!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.78,0:06:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.29,0:06:52.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.71,0:06:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.30,0:07:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You have forced Cao Xiong to death!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.58,0:07:10.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I would not, I would not!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.30,0:07:19.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, what will you do to Cao Zhi?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.99,0:07:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh no no no, mother, mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.83,0:07:32.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Your younger brother Cao Zhi has always loved wine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.64,0:07:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,It makes him unruly and careless.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.65,0:07:42.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Because he is proud of his talent, he is reckless.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.81,0:07:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,But you...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.24,0:07:54.15,Default,,0,0,0,,If you still remember your brotherhood, then you should spare his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.15,0:07:59.37,Default,,0,0,0,,This way, I can be at peace after my passing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.56,0:08:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother, I cherish his talent too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.50,0:08:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I hurt him?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.17,0:08:12.17,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Today, I just disciplined his arrogant temperament. Do not worry, mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.17,0:08:15.96,Default,,0,0,0,,That is good. That is good.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.96,0:08:17.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother, please rest easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.74,0:08:40.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, did the Lady Dowager try to convince you to spare Zijian?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.78,0:08:41.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.64,0:08:45.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijian is both talented and ambitious. \NWill he be willing to live under others?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.90,0:08:49.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Should he not be removed now, \Nhe will become a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.66,0:08:53.06,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2020,2380)\pos(286.4,478.4)}Huà Xīn\NStyled: Zǐyú
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.34,0:08:54.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot disobey my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.01,0:08:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,It is said Zijian is gifted with wit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.22,0:09:01.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not believe this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.11,0:09:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You can summon him and test his talents.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.06,0:09:10.81,Default,,0,0,0,,If he fails, kill him; if he passes, then demote him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.81,0:09:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,This can stop the mouths of the literati.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.26,0:09:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I, Cao Zhi, have come to apologize for my crimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.52,0:09:38.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You and I are brothers in affection, but lord and subject in justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.10,0:09:43.05,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you be arrogant and unreasonable?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.04,0:09:56.88,Default,,0,0,0,,When the former King was alive, you frequently boasted with your poetry and writing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.88,0:10:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I suspect someone else wrote for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.29,0:10:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, I demand that you think of a poem in seven steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.45,0:10:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,If you can do this, your life shall be spared.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.95,0:10:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,If not, then you will be punished without any mercy!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.76,0:10:23.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.89,0:10:43.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Is the Tiger Lord here?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.98,0:10:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.80,0:10:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,If he cannot make a poem in seven steps, cut him down!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.13,0:10:54.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Please name the topic.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.41,0:11:10.61,Default,,0,0,0,,We are brothers,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.36,0:11:14.53,Default,,0,0,0,,so let the topic be "brothers."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.53,0:11:18.39,Default,,0,0,0,,But the poem must not contain the word!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.92,0:11:39.89,Thinking,,0,0,0,,One step!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.64,0:11:46.04,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Two steps!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.88,0:11:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Beanstalks feed the bean-pot's flare,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.14,0:12:01.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Three steps!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.90,0:12:06.88,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Four steps!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.49,0:12:14.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}From that pot the beans would tear;
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.53,0:12:25.85,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Five steps!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.76,0:12:29.10,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Six steps!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.50,0:12:35.39,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Six steps!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.13,0:12:37.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"Born we are..."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.20,0:12:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"... from selfsame root,"
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.80,0:12:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"Why wish...”
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.91,0:12:48.14,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Seven steps!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.48,0:12:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"... to see the other sear?”
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.14,0:13:18.23,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,The Poem of Seven Steps (七步詩)\NBy Cao Zhi
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.85,0:13:23.56,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Beanstalks feed the bean-pot's flare,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.56,0:13:31.24,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}From that pot the beans would tear;
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.24,0:13:39.00,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"Born we are from selfsame root,"
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.00,0:13:45.52,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"Why wish to see the other sear?”
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.58,0:13:54.36,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Beanstalks feed the bean-pot's flare,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.36,0:14:02.07,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}From that pot the beans would tear;
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.07,0:14:08.74,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"Born we are from selfsame root,"
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.74,0:14:16.48,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"Why wish to see the other sear?”
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.39,0:14:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Since the King of Wei ascended to the throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.70,0:14:42.63,Default,,0,0,0,,his virtue has spread far and wide, \Nsurpassing the past and exceeding the present.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.63,0:14:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Not even Tang and Yu could compare to him!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.96,0:14:49.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The court has come to an agreement, the fate of the Han Dynasty is sealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.88,0:14:52.64,Default,,0,0,0,,We hope you will emulate the way of Yao and Shun
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.64,0:14:57.50,Default,,0,0,0,,by abdicating your throne and domain in favor of the King of Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.50,0:15:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,This way, the will of Heaven above and\N the will of people below shall be satiated.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.03,0:15:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty can also enjoy the fortune of leisure.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.81,0:15:13.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Your ancestors shall be fortunate, all those alive shall be fortunate.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.33,0:15:21.31,Default,,0,0,0,,We officials have agreed upon this\N and have come to make this petition.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.31,0:15:24.61,Default,,0,0,0,,We have come to make this petition!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.42,0:15:36.50,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1700,2100)\pos(316,486.4}Emperor Xiàn of Hàn
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.28,0:15:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,We petition that Your Majesty abdicate.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.24,0:15:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We petition that Your Majesty abdicate!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.06,0:15:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Ever since Emperor Gaozu slew the white serpent to begin an uprising,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.64,0:16:02.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\frx0\fry0}pacified Qin, destroyed Chu, \Nand built the nation for posterity.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.45,0:16:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Four hundred years of legacy, across so many generations!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.91,0:16:18.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Though We are not able, We have done no wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.30,0:16:24.59,Default,,0,0,0,,How could We dare abandon Our ancestors' foundations?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.74,0:16:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You need to discuss this matter again! Again!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.49,0:16:52.40,Default,,0,0,0,,If Your Majesty is unaware of the will of Heaven, you may ask these two men.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.05,0:16:59.16,Default,,0,0,0,,When the King of Wei came to power, a {\i1}Qilin{\i0} was born,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.16,0:17:01.64,Default,,0,0,0,,a phoenix came, and a golden dragon appeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.64,0:17:06.80,Default,,0,0,0,,These are auspicious signs from Heaven meaning that Wei shall succeed Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.52,0:17:10.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I am in charge of observing the Heavens.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.48,0:17:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,When I observed the night sky, I saw that the time of Han had expired.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.42,0:17:23.31,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: The Imperial Star (帝星): Known in the West as Kochab, or Beta Ursae Minoris. Formerly the North Pole star, it symbolized the emperor and his fortunes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.42,0:17:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The Imperial Star was dim,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.87,0:17:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,whereas the stars of Wei, from the highest of Heavens to the horizon, cannot be enumerated.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.46,0:17:28.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Moreover, there are prophecies. An omen states:
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.66,0:17:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"{\i1}Gǔi{\i0} is at the side; {\i1}wěi{\i0} is the leader."
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.57,0:17:33.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}They succeed the Han; no more needs to be said.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.93,0:17:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"{\i1}Yán{\i0} is at the east; {\i1}wǔ{\i0} is at the west."
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.04,0:17:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"Two joined {\i1}rì{\i0} move abreast."
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.64,0:17:42.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Because of this, Your Majesty should abdicate soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.43,0:17:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The aforesaid "{\i1}Gǔi{\i0} is at the side; {\i1}wěi{\i0} is the leader"
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.43,0:17:46.65,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: 委+鬼=魏
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.11,0:17:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}means the character {\i1}Wèi.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.81,0:17:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The aforesaid "{\i1}Yán{\i0} is at the east; {\i1}wǔ{\i0} is at the west"
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.81,0:17:53.45,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,言+午=許\N日+日=昌
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.93,0:17:53.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and "two joined {\i1}rì{\i0} move abreast" means {\i1}Xǔchāng.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.45,0:17:54.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.73,0:17:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Wei, which is at Xuchang, \Nshould accept the abdication of Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.92,0:18:02.48,Default,,0,0,0,,May Your Majesty consider this!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.03,0:18:07.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Omens and prophecies are but mere fantasy!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.91,0:18:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Why use fantasy to force Us to abandon Our ancestors' foundations?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.54,0:18:17.82,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1940,2260)\pos(310.4,465.6)}Wáng Lǎng\NStyled: Jǐngxīng
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.34,0:18:17.84,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, since times of antiquity,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.84,0:18:21.71,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,there shall be fall after rise and downfall after prosperity.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.71,0:18:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Was there ever a nation or house that has not fallen?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.96,0:18:30.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The Han Dynasty has lasted for over four hundred years. It is during your reign that its time has expired.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.76,0:18:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,It would be wise to leave without delay.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.47,0:18:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Any delays, and who knows what will happen? Who knows what will happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.86,0:18:42.79,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Oh yes! Your Majesty should retire, lest something will happen!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.79,0:18:49.17,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,The time of Han is over! Do not delay!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.17,0:18:53.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please hold the audience! Please hold the audience!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.14,0:18:55.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, the officials are urging for an audience.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.97,0:18:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, why are you refusing?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.24,0:19:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Your elder brother wants to usurp the dynasty, so he ordered the court to force me. I...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.30,0:19:09.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,7180,7540)\pos(291.2,404)}Empress Cáo
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.12,0:19:11.75,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare my elder brother do such a treasonous act?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.81,0:19:16.88,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,We ask Your Majesty to hold the audience.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.88,0:19:19.68,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,The officials are waiting in the great hall.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.17,0:19:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You traitors!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.57,0:19:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You dare rebel for riches and fortune?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.27,0:19:32.18,Default,,0,0,0,,My father's success was beyond measure, his renown known all over the realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.74,0:19:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet, he never dared to usurp the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.91,0:19:40.53,Default,,0,0,0,,My treacherous elder brother \N now dares to usurp the Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.49,0:19:43.52,Default,,0,0,0,,May Heaven curse him!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.78,0:20:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,We ask Your Majesty to attend court.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.02,0:20:04.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Now!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.50,0:20:31.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty may accept what we have discussed to avoid a calamity.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.16,0:20:36.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You have all received \Nthe bounty of the Han for so long.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.20,0:20:39.76,Default,,0,0,0,,How can you perform such disloyalty?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.76,0:20:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, if you will not accept the consensus,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.30,0:20:47.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I fear a disaster will arise at any moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.94,0:20:51.84,Default,,0,0,0,,It is not us being disloyal!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.18,0:20:59.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Who dares to murder me?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.21,0:21:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone in the world knows that you lack the blessings of being a ruler,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.59,0:21:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,hence the rampant chaos!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.39,0:21:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,If not for the King of Wei,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.95,0:21:12.32,Default,,0,0,0,,many would dare kill you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.45,0:21:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet, Your Majesty does not repay his kindness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.32,0:21:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Could it be that you want everyone to attack you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.66,0:21:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.83,0:21:31.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you abdicating or not? Speak!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.87,0:21:33.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Speak! Speak!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.62,0:21:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is the Guardian of the Jade Seal?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.40,0:21:38.16,Default,,0,0,0,,The Guardian of the Jade Seal is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.76,0:21:45.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hand over the Jade Seal!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.42,0:21:46.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Hand it over now!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.14,0:21:54.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,8260,8620)\pos(531.2,358.4)}Zǔ Bì
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.55,0:21:49.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The Jade Seal is property of the Son of Heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.02,0:21:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,How can a subject dare demand it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.49,0:21:53.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you handing it over or not?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.10,0:21:54.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Hand it over now!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.66,0:21:55.60,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.20,0:21:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Men, drag him out and execute him!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.98,0:21:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.49,0:22:02.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Traitor!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.16,0:22:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Traitors! Craven animals, all of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.49,0:22:15.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you abdicating or not? Speak!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.28,0:22:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Speak! Speak!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.03,0:22:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish to abdicate in favor of the King of Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.10,0:22:37.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, good.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.60,0:22:43.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The King of Wei will not fail Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.94,0:22:49.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Issue an edict now to reassure the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.26,0:23:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I thank that my last gasp is spared,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.23,0:23:11.49,Default,,0,0,0,,that I may live out my life in peace!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.74,0:23:19.21,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(1010.667,470.666)}Edict of \NAbdication
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.25,0:23:21.58,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Referring to the Five Elements of the Dynastic Cycle, in which each dynasty is represented by an element of the Wuxing. The Han Dynasty is thought to represent Fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.25,0:23:21.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The Phase of the Fire Virtue has ended.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.45,0:23:23.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Destiny is now ordained to the Cao Family.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.50,0:23:26.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The Sage has saith: When the Great Way is practiced, the world under Heaven belongs to all in equality.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.32,0:23:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The selfless Emperor Yao chose not his sons,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.32,0:23:30.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}thus his name has passed down in perpetuity.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.12,0:23:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}We have long envied and admired the way of Yao, \Nwhich We now choose to follow
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.56,0:23:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}by abdicating the throne to our chancellor, the King of Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.80,0:23:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.67,0:23:50.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4730,4970)\pos(311.2,472)}Sīmǎ Yí\NStyled: Zhòngdá
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.90,0:23:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.83,0:23:54.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Though the edict and the jade seal are here,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.18,0:23:57.08,Default,,0,0,0,,you should petition to politely decline them,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.08,0:24:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,to avoid inviting ire from the rest of the realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.63,0:24:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, good.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.73,0:24:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Men!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.30,0:24:10.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.32,0:24:13.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Have Wang Lang write a petition for me, saying I lack virtue
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.63,0:24:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,and ask to find a worthy man to succeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.57,0:24:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.16,0:24:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,The King of Wei refused the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.34,0:24:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What can we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.27,0:24:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,When King Wu of Wei accepted the title,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.53,0:24:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,he declined thrice before accepting once an edict prohibited such acts.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.56,0:24:40.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, you can issue the edict again. \NThe King of Wei will naturally accept it.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.49,0:24:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,If that is the case, We shall issue another edict.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.14,0:24:53.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty is wise in this matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.58,0:25:07.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Greetings, Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.45,0:25:10.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Rise!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.76,0:25:12.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.82,0:25:17.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.30,0:25:19.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.22,0:25:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.37,0:25:26.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, Emperor Xian has issued an edict of abdication for the second time.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.17,0:25:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Though it is the second edict, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.68,0:25:39.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Step down.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.66,0:25:40.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.22,0:25:49.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I fear that I leave the infamy of usurping the Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:50.73,0:25:52.98,Default,,0,0,0,,This is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.38,0:25:58.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Command the envoy to return with the edict and the jade seal again.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.42,0:26:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell Hua Xin to convince the Son of Heaven to build a platform for accepting abdication,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.53,0:26:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,choose an auspicious date, gather all the civil and martial officials,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.21,0:26:18.82,Default,,0,0,0,,and order the Son of Heaven to present the jade seal and abdicate in favor of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.82,0:26:23.58,Default,,0,0,0,,This way, suspicion may be cleared and stop the people from gossiping.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.31,0:27:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The Edict of Abdication!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.04,0:27:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The way of Han is failing, with the world losing order.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.31,0:27:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}When I inherited it, great chaos was rampant.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.99,0:27:20.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Warlords ran amok and the realm was in turmoil.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.50,0:27:24.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Due to the divine strength of King Wu of Wei, \Nthe land was saved from calamity.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.50,0:27:22.44,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: referring to Cao Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.40,0:27:27.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Many regions were pacified \Nand my ancestral temples were protected.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.68,0:27:29.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}How could I have been capable?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.38,0:27:32.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The entire domain is in his debt!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.37,0:27:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}You have succeeded him, \Nbringing glory to his virtue.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.25,0:27:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}You embody ideals both civil and martial, and honor the merits of your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.51,0:27:43.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The imperial spirits and gods have brought down omens.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.96,0:27:46.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}They all proclaim you fit to ascend.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.99,0:27:49.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The succession of Heaven falls upon you.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.66,0:27:51.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Do conform to this supreme ritual
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.88,0:27:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}so you may enjoy the world and inherit the Mandate of Heaven!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.86,0:28:53.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.90,0:29:13.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We decree:
Dialogue: 0,0:29:14.06,0:29:16.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The entire realm shall be pardoned!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.10,0:29:22.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The first year of the Yankang era shall\N be changed to the first year of the Huangchu era.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.10,0:29:22.06,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Huángchū (黃初)
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.06,0:29:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The name of the empire shall now be "Great Wei"!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.71,0:29:30.15,Default,,0,0,0,,The former King shall be known as "Tàizǔ Emperor Wu"!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.71,0:29:30.15,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Tàizǔ (太祖) = (Great) Ancestor
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.15,0:29:36.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.19,0:29:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! The sky cannot have two suns; the people cannot have two monarchs.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.60,0:29:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Since the Han emperor has abdicated, he should withdraw to his fief.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.36,0:29:56.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg for your sagacious decree:\N whence shall Mister Liu be settled?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.18,0:30:09.35,Default,,0,0,0,,We make Mister Liu the Duke of Shanyang.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.32,0:30:11.70,Default,,0,0,0,,He shall depart soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.70,0:30:13.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.89,0:30:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.27,0:30:31.65,Default,,0,0,0,,When an emperor is proclaimed, an emperor is deposed.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:31.65,0:30:34.16,Default,,0,0,0,,These are the ancient ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.16,0:30:37.76,Default,,0,0,0,,His Majesty does not hurt you out of mercy!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.76,0:30:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You are now made the Duke of Shanyang.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:40.33,0:30:45.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Be on your way now. Do not enter the court unless summoned!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.91,0:30:47.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Scram!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:48.33,0:31:03.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:04.01,0:31:07.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please thank Heaven and Earth!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:07.80,0:31:11.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please thank Heaven and Earth!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.96,0:32:08.39,Thinking,,0,0,0,,King Liu Bei of Hanzhong mourned for days after hearing Emperor Xian was murdered.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:08.39,0:32:12.46,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He ordered his officials to dress in mourning clothes and offer sacrifices.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.46,0:32:17.00,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He also gave him the \Nposthumous title of Emperor Xiaomin.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.48,0:32:17.00,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Xiàomǐn (孝愍): Filial and Missed
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.52,0:32:31.61,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei, sick from stress, could not govern.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.93,0:32:38.27,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang, who conferred with other officials,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.27,0:32:42.03,Thinking,,0,0,0,,said that the realm cannot be without a sovereign for even one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.03,0:32:47.34,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He made a memorial petitioning the King of Hanzhong to succeed to the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.46,0:32:44.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1860,2180)\pos(322,504)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.34,0:32:50.31,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei refused to comply.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.86,0:33:06.82,Thinking,,0,0,0,,For this, Zhuge Liang feigned sickness and refused to leave his home.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.00,0:33:27.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, the King of Hanzhong is paying a visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.02,0:33:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Help me up.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.46,0:33:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, lie down.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.76,0:33:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, lie down.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.45,0:33:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Forgive me for my rudeness.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.74,0:33:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, what are you sick with?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.63,0:33:49.99,Default,,0,0,0,,A burning anguish. My life will soon end.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.45,0:33:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, what is bothering you?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.91,0:33:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Please tell me, Strategos.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.45,0:34:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, what problem has made you sick?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.56,0:34:13.22,Default,,0,0,0,,We, as ruler and minister, are one and the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.22,0:34:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What concern cannot be told to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.77,0:34:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Ever since I left the thatched hut and met Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:22.97,0:34:26.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I have followed you to the present and you have always heeded me.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.78,0:34:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness now has the Riverlands, just as I said long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.42,0:34:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I am where I am today because of you, Strategos!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.46,0:34:46.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi has now usurped the Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.10,0:34:48.97,Default,,0,0,0,,The dynasty will soon be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.12,0:34:52.74,Default,,0,0,0,,All the civil and martial officials wish to proclaim you the new emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.61,0:34:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,They want to destroy Wei, revive the House of Liu, \Nand seek the great enterprise with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.15,0:35:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet, Your Highness keeps on refusing.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.58,0:35:08.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The disgruntled officials will disperse soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.79,0:35:17.88,Default,,0,0,0,,If the officials do so and Wu and Wei attack, the Riverlands will be in danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.88,0:35:20.99,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I not be anxious?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:24.33,0:35:26.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I am not declining.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.48,0:35:29.97,Default,,0,0,0,,My second brother is not yet avenged. How can I take the throne?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.97,0:35:33.74,Default,,0,0,0,,As the Sage said, "If what in name is improper, then its meaning is dishonest."
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.74,0:35:38.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, Your Highness is true in both name and meaning. Why talk any further?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.68,0:35:43.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you not heard that "what Heaven grants is refused only at peril"?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.22,0:35:50.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine, when you recover, it will not be too late to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:51.20,0:35:52.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.24,0:36:04.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.94,0:36:09.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.45,0:36:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.45,0:36:18.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Since you have agreed to assume the throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.07,0:36:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,please select an auspicious date to conduct the ceremony.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.69,0:36:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Please select an auspicious date to conduct the ceremony!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.36,0:36:32.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You have forced me into a dishonorable position!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.92,0:36:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The Strategos is not ill!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.52,0:36:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,As the request is granted,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.92,0:36:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,build an altar to conduct the\N ceremony on the auspicious day!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.62,0:36:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Please conduct the ceremony!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:47.01,0:37:49.17,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei climbed the ritual altar,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:49.17,0:37:52.65,Thinking,,0,0,0,,receiving the imperial jade seal, \Nand was enthroned as Emperor of new Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.94,0:37:57.98,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(324.8,478.4)}Liú Shàn\NStyled: Gōngsì
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.65,0:37:57.81,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He changed the era to Zhangwu and made Liu Shan the Crown Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.65,0:37:57.81,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Zhāngwǔ = 章武
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.96,0:38:02.19,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He named Zhuge Liang as Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:05.53,0:38:09.10,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Xu Jing was made the Minister of the Masses.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:06.06,0:38:08.06,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1700,1980)\pos(308.8,496)}Xǔ Jìng\NStyled: Wénxiú
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.10,0:38:12.34,Thinking,,0,0,0,,All officials were given promotions and rewards,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.34,0:38:14.26,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and a general pardon was issued.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.26,0:38:17.92,Thinking,,0,0,0,,The people of the Riverlands all rejoiced.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.68,0:38:30.07,Default,,0,0,0,,We swore the fraternal oath\N at the Peach Garden with Guan and Zhang,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.07,0:38:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,swearing to live and die together.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:32.89,0:38:37.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Sadly, Yunchang, Our second brother, \Nwas murdered by Sun Quan of Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.64,0:38:40.32,Default,,0,0,0,,If he is not avenged,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.10,0:38:43.22,Default,,0,0,0,,then the oath would be broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.26,0:38:44.42,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2780,3140)\pos(353.6,505.6)}Zhào Yún\NStyled: Zǐlóng
Dialogue: 0,0:38:47.87,0:38:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,We intend to raise our entire army to attack Eastern Wu and capture Sun Quan.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:55.00,0:38:56.88,Default,,0,0,0,,This would clear my grudge.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.88,0:38:57.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.22,0:38:59.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You must not!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:01.18,0:39:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, the enemy of the nation is Cao Cao, not Sun Quan!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.76,0:39:11.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that Cao Pi has usurped the Han and angered the world, you should make Guanzhong the target.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.06,0:39:13.63,Default,,0,0,0,,The army should be at the upper Wei river to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:13.63,0:39:17.73,Default,,0,0,0,,This way, the righteous east of the passes will welcome us with grain.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.33,0:39:22.10,Default,,0,0,0,,If Wu is attacked instead of Wei, how can the engaged forces return quickly?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:22.87,0:39:25.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Please consider this carefully, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:29.60,0:39:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sun Quan murdered Our younger brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.08,0:39:42.74,Default,,0,0,0,,We hold great hatred for Fu Shiren, \NMi Fang, Pan Zhang, and Ma Zhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.53,0:39:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Only by gnawing on their flesh and \Nexterminating their clans can We satiate Our anger.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.45,0:39:51.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Dear liegeman, why are you against Us?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:52.31,0:39:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,The enmity against the traitors of Han is public,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.85,0:39:56.93,Default,,0,0,0,,but the enmity for brothers is personal.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.81,0:40:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that Your Majesty will prioritize the empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:00.95,0:40:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,If we cannot avenge my younger brother,\N then what value do thousands of {\i1}li{\i0} have?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:09.30,0:40:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,That...
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.79,0:40:20.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please ruminate over\N what Zilong said before taking action!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.26,0:40:21.98,Default,,0,0,0,,My mind is set.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:22.76,0:40:24.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not protest any further.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.46,0:40:34.34,Default,,0,0,0,,We order the three armies to raise troops to attack Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.34,0:40:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:35.78,0:40:40.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Send an envoy to the west of Wu to \Nborrow fifty thousand warriors of the southern tribes.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.08,0:40:43.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Also, send an envoy to Langzhong to deliver the edict to Zhang Fei!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:43.89,0:40:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Comment: 0,0:16:56.05,0:16:59.16,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Qílín （麒麟）: A legendary beast with the shape of a deer, the tail of an ox, a single horn, and covered with scales. Said to bring an auspicious sign.
Comment: 0,0:32:00.96,0:32:08.39,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Emperor Xian, in fact, died much later, in 234 CE.

